IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `soca-dates`
IMPORT `soca-core`
IMPORT `soca-seat`

-- Survival of Causes of Action Act 1940 (SA) -- cases for the claimant's seat (soca-seat.l4), with a few on the
-- soca-core.l4 and soca-dates.l4 functions the seat composes (s 3(3) and the Schedule, the s 4(b) trace, the month
-- arithmetic). Every expected value was worked by hand from the deposited text (the section is named on each group),
-- never copied from the encoding's output. Edges: the last day of each six months, the day after, month ends and leap
-- years (fork F1), proceedings taken before the grant (fork F2), each limb of s 3(2) and s 4.
--
-- BASELINE ENCODING. Not for public use as advice. See NOTES.md.

§ `Cases: the claimant`

-- Short names for the answers.
`survives for` MEANS `yes: the cause of action survives for the benefit of the estate of the person who died (s 2(1)(a))`
`defamation for` MEANS `no: a cause of action in defamation does not survive for the estate (s 2(2))`
`not vested` MEANS `not covered: s 2(1)(a) speaks only of a cause of action vested in the person at the time of death`
`survives against` MEANS `yes: the cause of action survives against the estate of the person who died (s 2(1)(b))`
`survives by s 5` MEANS `yes: the person who died before or with the damage is deemed to have been liable before death, and the cause of action survives against the estate (ss 5, 2(1)(b))`
`defamation against` MEANS `no: a cause of action in defamation does not survive against the estate (s 2(2))`
`none against` MEANS `not covered: s 2(1)(b) and s 5 speak only of a cause of action existing against the person at death, or one that would have existed had they not died before or with the damage`

`no estate claim` MEANS `no: the estate does not recover it, because the cause of action does not survive for the benefit of the estate (s 2)`
`excluded a` MEANS `no: s 3(1)(a) excludes it from the damages recoverable for the benefit of the estate`
`excluded iv` MEANS `no: s 3(1)(a)(iv) excludes earnings for the years lost, and the dust-related condition exception in s 3(2) does not restore them`
`excluded b` MEANS `no: s 3(1)(b) excludes exemplary damages`
`dust yes` MEANS `yes: s 3(2) lets the estate recover it, because the person started an action for a dust-related condition and died of that condition before the action was finally determined`
`excluded d` MEANS `no: the wrong caused the death, so the damages are calculated without reference to a loss or gain to the estate consequent on the death (s 3(1)(d))`
`funeral` MEANS `yes, it may be included: the wrong caused the death, and a sum for funeral expenses may be included (s 3(1)(d))`
`not excluded` MEANS `s 3 does not exclude it: the estate recovers it as the general law of damages allows`
`d silent` MEANS `not covered: s 3(1)(d) applies only where the wrong caused the death; the Act does not otherwise deal with it`

`would keep` MEANS `yes: if you die of it before your action is finally determined, your estate recovers damages for pain and suffering, bodily and mental harm, curtailment of expectation of life, and exemplary damages (s 3(2))`
`not commenced` MEANS `not yet: s 3(2) applies only once you have commenced an action for damages for the condition`
`not dust` MEANS `no: it is not a dust-related condition (s 3(3)), so s 3(2) does not apply and s 3(1) excludes those damages from what your estate recovers`

`p defamation` MEANS `no: a cause of action in defamation does not survive, so there is nothing to sue the estate on (s 2(2))`
`p none` MEANS `not covered: no cause of action existed against the person at death, and s 5 does not apply`
`p not tort` MEANS `s 4 does not apply: the cause of action is not in tort; it survives against the estate (s 2(1)(b)) and s 4 sets no condition on it`
`p pending` MEANS `yes: proceedings against the person were pending at the date of death (s 4(a))`
`p too early` MEANS `no: the cause of action arose more than six months before the death and no proceedings were pending at the death, so no proceedings are maintainable (s 4)`
`p no grant` MEANS `not yet: the six months in s 4(b) have not begun, because no probate or letters of administration have been taken out`
`p in time` MEANS `yes: the cause of action arose not earlier than six months before the death and proceedings were taken not later than six months after the grant (s 4(b))`
`p still` MEANS `still in time: proceedings must be taken not later than six months after the grant (s 4(b))`
`p late` MEANS `no: proceedings were not taken within six months after the grant, so no proceedings are maintainable (s 4(b))`

`dep no` MEANS `no: this Act does not take away the dependants' right to bring an action for the death (s 6(1)); that action is separate from the estate's surviving claim`
`dep none` MEANS `not covered: s 6(1) speaks only of the dependants of the person who died`
`cn yes` MEANS `yes: the Law Reform (Contributory Negligence and Apportionment of Liability) Act 2001 applies to the surviving cause of action (s 6(2))`
`cn none` MEANS `not covered: s 6(2) speaks only of a cause of action that survives for or against an estate under this Act`

`other` MEANS `another condition`
`lungs` MEANS `another condition of the lungs, pleura or peritoneum`

§§ `s 2(1)(a), (2): the claim of the person who died`

#ASSERT `Does the claim of the person who died survive for their estate` TRUE FALSE EQUALS `survives for`
#ASSERT `Does the claim of the person who died survive for their estate` TRUE TRUE EQUALS `defamation for`
#ASSERT `Does the claim of the person who died survive for their estate` FALSE FALSE EQUALS `not vested`
-- no cause of action at all: the defamation flag is moot.
#ASSERT `Does the claim of the person who died survive for their estate` FALSE TRUE EQUALS `not vested`

§§ `ss 2(1)(b), (2), 5: a claim against a person who died`

-- inputs: existed at death, damage after or at death, would have subsisted had they not died first, defamation
#ASSERT `Does my claim survive against the estate of the person who died` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `survives against`
#ASSERT `Does my claim survive against the estate of the person who died` FALSE TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS `survives by s 5`
-- s 5 needs both limbs.
#ASSERT `Does my claim survive against the estate of the person who died` FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `none against`
#ASSERT `Does my claim survive against the estate of the person who died` FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE EQUALS `none against`
#ASSERT `Does my claim survive against the estate of the person who died` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `none against`
#ASSERT `Does my claim survive against the estate of the person who died` TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE EQUALS `defamation against`
-- s 5's deeming is "for the purposes of this Act", so s 2(2) still bars defamation.
#ASSERT `Does my claim survive against the estate of the person who died` FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS `defamation against`
-- existing at death is answered under s 2(1)(b) even if the s 5 facts are also given.
#ASSERT `Does my claim survive against the estate of the person who died` TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS `survives against`

§§ `s 3(3) and the Schedule: dust-related condition`

#ASSERT `is a prescribed dust disease (Schedule)` `aluminosis`
#ASSERT `is a prescribed dust disease (Schedule)` `asbestosis`
#ASSERT `is a prescribed dust disease (Schedule)` `asbestos induced carcinoma`
#ASSERT `is a prescribed dust disease (Schedule)` `asbestos related pleural diseases`
#ASSERT `is a prescribed dust disease (Schedule)` `bagassosis`
#ASSERT `is a prescribed dust disease (Schedule)` `berylliosis`
#ASSERT `is a prescribed dust disease (Schedule)` `byssinosis`
#ASSERT `is a prescribed dust disease (Schedule)` `coal dust pneumoconiosis`
#ASSERT `is a prescribed dust disease (Schedule)` `farmers lung`
#ASSERT `is a prescribed dust disease (Schedule)` `hard metal pneumoconiosis`
#ASSERT `is a prescribed dust disease (Schedule)` `mesothelioma`
#ASSERT `is a prescribed dust disease (Schedule)` `silicosis`
#ASSERT `is a prescribed dust disease (Schedule)` `silico-tuberculosis`
#ASSERT `is a prescribed dust disease (Schedule)` `talcosis`
#ASSERT (NOT (`is a prescribed dust disease (Schedule)` `lungs`))
#ASSERT (NOT (`is a prescribed dust disease (Schedule)` `other`))
-- (a): a Schedule disease needs no showing that dust caused it.
#ASSERT `is a dust-related condition (s 3(3))` `mesothelioma` FALSE
-- (b): another lung, pleura or peritoneum condition only if attributable to dust.
#ASSERT `is a dust-related condition (s 3(3))` `lungs` TRUE
#ASSERT (NOT (`is a dust-related condition (s 3(3))` `lungs` FALSE))
-- a condition elsewhere in the body is outside (b) even if dust caused it.
#ASSERT (NOT (`is a dust-related condition (s 3(3))` `other` TRUE))

§§ `s 3(1): the heads of damages, ordinary case (the wrong caused the death, no dust condition)`

-- inputs: head, vested, defamation, the wrong caused the death, condition, attributable to dust, commenced, died of it, finally determined
#ASSERT `Can the estate recover this kind of damages` `pain or suffering` TRUE FALSE TRUE `other` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `excluded a`
#ASSERT `Can the estate recover this kind of damages` `bodily or mental harm` TRUE FALSE TRUE `other` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `excluded a`
#ASSERT `Can the estate recover this kind of damages` `the curtailment of expectation of life` TRUE FALSE TRUE `other` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `excluded a`
#ASSERT `Can the estate recover this kind of damages` `loss of earning capacity or future earnings for the years lost` TRUE FALSE TRUE `other` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `excluded iv`
#ASSERT `Can the estate recover this kind of damages` `exemplary damages` TRUE FALSE TRUE `other` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `excluded b`
#ASSERT `Can the estate recover this kind of damages` `funeral expenses` TRUE FALSE TRUE `other` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `funeral`
#ASSERT `Can the estate recover this kind of damages` `a loss or gain to the estate consequent on the death` TRUE FALSE TRUE `other` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `excluded d`
#ASSERT `Can the estate recover this kind of damages` `other damages` TRUE FALSE TRUE `other` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `not excluded`

§§ `s 3(1): the wrong did not cause the death`

#ASSERT `Can the estate recover this kind of damages` `pain or suffering` TRUE FALSE FALSE `other` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `excluded a`
#ASSERT `Can the estate recover this kind of damages` `exemplary damages` TRUE FALSE FALSE `other` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `excluded b`
#ASSERT `Can the estate recover this kind of damages` `funeral expenses` TRUE FALSE FALSE `other` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `d silent`
#ASSERT `Can the estate recover this kind of damages` `a loss or gain to the estate consequent on the death` TRUE FALSE FALSE `other` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `d silent`
#ASSERT `Can the estate recover this kind of damages` `other damages` TRUE FALSE FALSE `other` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `not excluded`

§§ `s 3(1): no surviving claim`

#ASSERT `Can the estate recover this kind of damages` `other damages` FALSE FALSE TRUE `other` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `no estate claim`
#ASSERT `Can the estate recover this kind of damages` `funeral expenses` TRUE TRUE TRUE `other` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `no estate claim`
-- even the s 3(2) facts do not help a claim that does not survive.
#ASSERT `Can the estate recover this kind of damages` `pain or suffering` FALSE FALSE TRUE `mesothelioma` FALSE TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS `no estate claim`

§§ `s 3(2): the dust-related condition exception (mesothelioma; action commenced; died of it before final determination)`

#ASSERT `Can the estate recover this kind of damages` `pain or suffering` TRUE FALSE TRUE `mesothelioma` FALSE TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS `dust yes`
#ASSERT `Can the estate recover this kind of damages` `bodily or mental harm` TRUE FALSE TRUE `mesothelioma` FALSE TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS `dust yes`
#ASSERT `Can the estate recover this kind of damages` `the curtailment of expectation of life` TRUE FALSE TRUE `mesothelioma` FALSE TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS `dust yes`
#ASSERT `Can the estate recover this kind of damages` `exemplary damages` TRUE FALSE TRUE `mesothelioma` FALSE TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS `dust yes`
-- s 3(2) does not name (iv): the lost years stay excluded.
#ASSERT `Can the estate recover this kind of damages` `loss of earning capacity or future earnings for the years lost` TRUE FALSE TRUE `mesothelioma` FALSE TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS `excluded iv`
#ASSERT `Can the estate recover this kind of damages` `funeral expenses` TRUE FALSE TRUE `mesothelioma` FALSE TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS `funeral`
#ASSERT `Can the estate recover this kind of damages` `a loss or gain to the estate consequent on the death` TRUE FALSE TRUE `mesothelioma` FALSE TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS `excluded d`
-- each limb of s 3(2) failing in turn. The action was finally determined before death:
#ASSERT `Can the estate recover this kind of damages` `pain or suffering` TRUE FALSE TRUE `mesothelioma` FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS `excluded a`
-- no action commenced in life:
#ASSERT `Can the estate recover this kind of damages` `pain or suffering` TRUE FALSE TRUE `mesothelioma` FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE EQUALS `excluded a`
-- died of something else:
#ASSERT `Can the estate recover this kind of damages` `exemplary damages` TRUE FALSE FALSE `mesothelioma` FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `excluded b`
-- (b) limb: another lung condition attributable to dust, then not attributable, then a condition elsewhere:
#ASSERT `Can the estate recover this kind of damages` `pain or suffering` TRUE FALSE TRUE `lungs` TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS `dust yes`
#ASSERT `Can the estate recover this kind of damages` `pain or suffering` TRUE FALSE TRUE `lungs` FALSE TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS `excluded a`
#ASSERT `Can the estate recover this kind of damages` `pain or suffering` TRUE FALSE TRUE `other` TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS `excluded a`
-- a Schedule disease other than mesothelioma:
#ASSERT `Can the estate recover this kind of damages` `the curtailment of expectation of life` TRUE FALSE TRUE `silicosis` FALSE TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS `dust yes`

§§ `s 3(2) asked in life`

#ASSERT `Will my estate keep those damages if I die of my dust disease` `asbestosis` FALSE TRUE EQUALS `would keep`
#ASSERT `Will my estate keep those damages if I die of my dust disease` `asbestosis` FALSE FALSE EQUALS `not commenced`
#ASSERT `Will my estate keep those damages if I die of my dust disease` `lungs` TRUE TRUE EQUALS `would keep`
#ASSERT `Will my estate keep those damages if I die of my dust disease` `lungs` FALSE TRUE EQUALS `not dust`
#ASSERT `Will my estate keep those damages if I die of my dust disease` `other` TRUE TRUE EQUALS `not dust`

§§ `Dates (fork F1): six months before the death, six months after the grant`

#ASSERT `What is the earliest day my claim against the estate may have arisen` (`the date` 15 3 2026) EQUALS `the date` 15 9 2025
#ASSERT `What is the earliest day my claim against the estate may have arisen` (`the date` 15 1 2026) EQUALS `the date` 15 7 2025
#ASSERT `What is the earliest day my claim against the estate may have arisen` (`the date` 31 8 2025) EQUALS `the date` 28 2 2025
#ASSERT `What is the earliest day my claim against the estate may have arisen` (`the date` 31 8 2024) EQUALS `the date` 29 2 2024
#ASSERT `By when must I take proceedings against the estate` (`the date` 10 10 2026) EQUALS `the date` 10 4 2027
#ASSERT `By when must I take proceedings against the estate` (`the date` 31 8 2025) EQUALS `the date` 28 2 2026
#ASSERT `By when must I take proceedings against the estate` (`the date` 31 8 2027) EQUALS `the date` 29 2 2028
#ASSERT `By when must I take proceedings against the estate` (`the date` 15 8 2025) EQUALS `the date` 15 2 2026
#ASSERT `By when must I take proceedings against the estate` (`the date` 30 6 2026) EQUALS `the date` 30 12 2026

§§ `s 4(b) as a regulative rule (grant 10 October 2026; last day 10 April 2027)`

#ASSERT `were proceedings taken within six months after the grant (s 4(b))` (`the date` 10 10 2026) TRUE (`the date` 10 4 2027) (`the date` 1 1 2030) EQUALS `in time`
#ASSERT `were proceedings taken within six months after the grant (s 4(b))` (`the date` 10 10 2026) TRUE (`the date` 11 4 2027) (`the date` 1 1 2030) EQUALS `out of time`
#ASSERT `were proceedings taken within six months after the grant (s 4(b))` (`the date` 10 10 2026) TRUE (`the date` 11 10 2026) (`the date` 1 1 2030) EQUALS `in time`
#ASSERT `were proceedings taken within six months after the grant (s 4(b))` (`the date` 10 10 2026) FALSE (`the date` 1 1 2000) (`the date` 10 4 2027) EQUALS `still in time`
#ASSERT `were proceedings taken within six months after the grant (s 4(b))` (`the date` 10 10 2026) FALSE (`the date` 1 1 2000) (`the date` 11 4 2027) EQUALS `out of time`
-- fork F2: proceedings taken on or before the grant are "not later than six months after" it.
#ASSERT `were proceedings taken within six months after the grant (s 4(b))` (`the date` 10 10 2026) TRUE (`the date` 10 10 2026) (`the date` 1 1 2030) EQUALS `in time`
#ASSERT `were proceedings taken within six months after the grant (s 4(b))` (`the date` 10 10 2026) TRUE (`the date` 1 6 2026) (`the date` 1 1 2030) EQUALS `in time`
#ASSERT `were proceedings taken within six months after the grant (s 4(b))` (`the date` 10 10 2026) FALSE (`the date` 1 1 2000) (`the date` 1 6 2026) EQUALS `still in time`
-- the rule itself, traced: 182 days from 10 October 2026 to 10 April 2027.
#ASSERT `the days from` (`the date` 10 10 2026) `to` (`the date` 10 4 2027) EQUALS 182
GIVEN `the day taken` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `proceedings on day fulfil the 182-day rule` `the day taken` IF
    CONSIDER EVALTRACE (`s 4(b) -- proceedings must be taken not later than six months after the grant` 182) 0 (LIST (EVENT `the claimant` `take proceedings against the estate` `the day taken`))
    WHEN FULFILLED THEN TRUE
    OTHERWISE FALSE

#ASSERT `proceedings on day fulfil the 182-day rule` 182
#ASSERT `proceedings on day fulfil the 182-day rule` 1
#ASSERT (NOT (`proceedings on day fulfil the 182-day rule` 183))

§§ `s 4: can I still sue the estate`

-- inputs: existed, damage after, would have subsisted, defamation, tort, pending, arose, death, grant taken, grant day, taken, day taken, today
-- Base: negligence claim arising 1 September 2025, death 1 March 2026 (earliest day 1 September 2025), grant 10 October 2026 (last day 10 April 2027).
#ASSERT `Can I still sue the estate` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE (`the date` 1 9 2025) (`the date` 1 3 2026) TRUE (`the date` 10 10 2026) TRUE (`the date` 10 4 2027) (`the date` 1 5 2027) EQUALS `p in time`
#ASSERT `Can I still sue the estate` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE (`the date` 1 9 2025) (`the date` 1 3 2026) TRUE (`the date` 10 10 2026) TRUE (`the date` 11 4 2027) (`the date` 1 5 2027) EQUALS `p late`
#ASSERT `Can I still sue the estate` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE (`the date` 1 9 2025) (`the date` 1 3 2026) TRUE (`the date` 10 10 2026) FALSE (`the date` 1 1 2000) (`the date` 10 4 2027) EQUALS `p still`
#ASSERT `Can I still sue the estate` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE (`the date` 1 9 2025) (`the date` 1 3 2026) TRUE (`the date` 10 10 2026) FALSE (`the date` 1 1 2000) (`the date` 11 4 2027) EQUALS `p late`
-- arose one day before the earliest day: barred, whatever the timing of proceedings.
#ASSERT `Can I still sue the estate` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE (`the date` 31 8 2025) (`the date` 1 3 2026) TRUE (`the date` 10 10 2026) TRUE (`the date` 1 11 2026) (`the date` 1 12 2026) EQUALS `p too early`
-- (a) proceedings pending at death: maintainable however early it arose.
#ASSERT `Can I still sue the estate` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE (`the date` 1 1 2020) (`the date` 1 3 2026) FALSE (`the date` 1 1 2000) FALSE (`the date` 1 1 2000) (`the date` 1 1 2030) EQUALS `p pending`
-- no grant yet: the six months have not begun.
#ASSERT `Can I still sue the estate` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE (`the date` 1 9 2025) (`the date` 1 3 2026) FALSE (`the date` 1 1 2000) FALSE (`the date` 1 1 2000) (`the date` 1 1 2030) EQUALS `p no grant`
-- fork F2: proceedings taken before the grant.
#ASSERT `Can I still sue the estate` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE (`the date` 1 9 2025) (`the date` 1 3 2026) TRUE (`the date` 10 10 2026) TRUE (`the date` 1 6 2026) (`the date` 1 1 2030) EQUALS `p in time`
-- not in tort (for example contract): s 4 sets no condition.
#ASSERT `Can I still sue the estate` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE (`the date` 1 1 2020) (`the date` 1 3 2026) TRUE (`the date` 10 10 2026) TRUE (`the date` 1 1 2030) (`the date` 1 1 2030) EQUALS `p not tort`
#ASSERT `Can I still sue the estate` TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE FALSE (`the date` 1 9 2025) (`the date` 1 3 2026) TRUE (`the date` 10 10 2026) TRUE (`the date` 1 11 2026) (`the date` 1 12 2026) EQUALS `p defamation`
#ASSERT `Can I still sue the estate` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE (`the date` 1 9 2025) (`the date` 1 3 2026) TRUE (`the date` 10 10 2026) TRUE (`the date` 1 11 2026) (`the date` 1 12 2026) EQUALS `p none`
-- s 5: a crash that killed the driver and injured you on the same day; the damage arose on the day of death.
#ASSERT `Can I still sue the estate` FALSE TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE (`the date` 1 3 2026) (`the date` 1 3 2026) TRUE (`the date` 10 10 2026) TRUE (`the date` 1 11 2026) (`the date` 1 12 2026) EQUALS `p in time`
#ASSERT `Can I still sue the estate` FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE (`the date` 1 3 2026) (`the date` 1 3 2026) TRUE (`the date` 10 10 2026) TRUE (`the date` 1 11 2026) (`the date` 1 12 2026) EQUALS `p none`
-- month-end grant: 31 August 2025, last day 28 February 2026.
#ASSERT `Can I still sue the estate` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE (`the date` 1 6 2025) (`the date` 1 7 2025) TRUE (`the date` 31 8 2025) TRUE (`the date` 28 2 2026) (`the date` 1 3 2026) EQUALS `p in time`
#ASSERT `Can I still sue the estate` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE (`the date` 1 6 2025) (`the date` 1 7 2025) TRUE (`the date` 31 8 2025) TRUE (`the date` 1 3 2026) (`the date` 1 3 2026) EQUALS `p late`
-- month-end death: 31 August 2025, earliest day 28 February 2025.
#ASSERT `Can I still sue the estate` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE (`the date` 28 2 2025) (`the date` 31 8 2025) TRUE (`the date` 1 10 2025) TRUE (`the date` 1 11 2025) (`the date` 1 12 2025) EQUALS `p in time`
#ASSERT `Can I still sue the estate` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE (`the date` 27 2 2025) (`the date` 31 8 2025) TRUE (`the date` 1 10 2025) TRUE (`the date` 1 11 2025) (`the date` 1 12 2025) EQUALS `p too early`

§§ `s 6(1): dependants`

#ASSERT `Does the surviving claim affect my claim for the death` TRUE EQUALS `dep no`
#ASSERT `Does the surviving claim affect my claim for the death` FALSE EQUALS `dep none`

§§ `s 6(2): contributory negligence and apportionment`

-- inputs: whose claim, existed at death, damage after, would have subsisted, defamation
#ASSERT `Does the contributory negligence Act apply to the surviving claim` `the claim of the person who died` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `cn yes`
#ASSERT `Does the contributory negligence Act apply to the surviving claim` `the claim of the person who died` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `cn none`
#ASSERT `Does the contributory negligence Act apply to the surviving claim` `the claim of the person who died` TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE EQUALS `cn none`
-- s 5 is for claims against a person who died; it does not make the deceased's own claim survive.
#ASSERT `Does the contributory negligence Act apply to the surviving claim` `the claim of the person who died` FALSE TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS `cn none`
#ASSERT `Does the contributory negligence Act apply to the surviving claim` `a claim against the person who died` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `cn yes`
#ASSERT `Does the contributory negligence Act apply to the surviving claim` `a claim against the person who died` FALSE TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS `cn yes`
#ASSERT `Does the contributory negligence Act apply to the surviving claim` `a claim against the person who died` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `cn none`
#ASSERT `Does the contributory negligence Act apply to the surviving claim` `a claim against the person who died` TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE EQUALS `cn none`
